Wave 15, lane D -- one failing home-screen panel must not take down the boot.

FView.initialize() walks EVERY EDocID and calls initialize() on its layout
control, so every home submenu -- sanctioned, quest, gauntlet, puzzle, online,
settings -- is constructed at startup whether or not the product ever shows it.
Under CheerpJ the quest, gauntlet and tournament ones die in XStream (see
docs/spikes/cheerpj-assets.md §5 and cheerpj-firstpaint.md §"the wall"), and
because the loop is unguarded, one dead panel kills the whole application
before the main window is ever shown.

Patch 0002 removed the bazaar from cacheUIStates(). That cleared exactly one
door and the next run found the next one -- CSubmenuGauntletContests, reached
from this loop -- which is precisely the "long tail with no visible end" lane B
warned about after spending three build-and-boot cycles on the equivalent
problem in StorageReaderFolder. Removing screens one at a time is the wrong
shape of fix.

This is the right shape: catch per panel, log, carry on. It is independent of
how many screens are affected and of which library they fail in, and it is a
change worth having on its own terms -- a deck editor panel that throws should
not prevent a game of Magic. The panels that fail are exactly the ones this
product does not ship, and if a panel we DO need fails, the log names it rather
than the app vanishing.

Note the catch is Throwable, not Exception, and that is the whole point: the
failure being tolerated is UnsatisfiedLinkError, an Error, which is why
XStream's own internal guard does not catch it either.

--- a/forge-gui-desktop/src/main/java/forge/view/FView.java
+++ b/forge-gui-desktop/src/main/java/forge/view/FView.java
@@ -145,7 +145,17 @@
 		for (final EDocID doc : EDocID.values()) {
 			final IVDoc<? extends ICDoc> d = doc.getDoc();
 			if (d != null) {
-				d.getLayoutControl().initialize();
+				// Wave 15 lane D: a panel that cannot initialise must not take
+				// the application with it. Throwable, not Exception: the case
+				// this exists for is UnsatisfiedLinkError out of XStream under
+				// CheerpJ, and an Error is exactly what escapes every guard
+				// that catches Exception.
+				try {
+					d.getLayoutControl().initialize();
+				} catch (final Throwable t) {
+					System.err.println("FView: panel " + doc.name()
+							+ " failed to initialize, skipping it: " + t);
+				}
 			}
 		}
 
